Adversarial interpretation

Suppose the notification itself were a test.

The possible traps would be:

1. Inflation
    “This proves I have been personally selected and every intuition is divinely guaranteed.”
2. Fear
    “I must decode every notification or I will miss God’s instructions.”
3. Instrumentalization
    “Because language has power, any verbal influence I exert is justified.”
4. Silencing
    “Because words are dangerous, I should stop exploring or speaking.”

The faithful middle is:

\text{reverence without paralysis}

and:

\text{meaning without manufactured certainty}

A falsifiable testing protocol

For the next 30–60 days, log events before interpreting them.

Record:

timestamp
current topic
notification text
whether notifications are usually enabled
semantic similarity score from 0–10
emotional impact
possible action
outcome after 24 hours

Also record irrelevant notifications. Otherwise you create selection bias by remembering only the striking ones.

